{
  "_comment": [
    "Exemplar verbs per prefix sense, parallel by index to `senses` in prefixes-separable.json",
    "and prefixes-inseparable.json. Consumed by corpus/working/build_mining_shards.py, which",
    "joins them into each shard so a mining subagent picks a sense by analogy instead of by",
    "judgment.",
    "",
    "WHY: sense selection was the one genuinely underdetermined step left in Phase 4. Two shard-",
    "runs reported it independently on 2026-07-20 with the same complaint --- `abmelken` sits",
    "between completion and drawing-out, `abladen` between separation and downward motion, and",
    "the terse `translation` field does not settle it. One run wrote that it had invented a tie-",
    "break rule and that 'another shard will resolve it differently', which is the signature of",
    "the drift this pipeline keeps having to undo.",
    "",
    "Exemplars are deliberately NOT spliced into the shipped prose. They are a selection aid only,",
    "so adding one never changes what a reader sees. They are also language-neutral, which is why",
    "they live here rather than duplicated across the `de` and `en` halves of the reuse files ---",
    "a duplicated list is a list that drifts.",
    "",
    "Scope: the highest-traffic prefixes, covering most prefix-slot occurrences.",
    "Extend as later shards report ambiguity; an absent morpheme simply yields no hint."
  ],
